Description: CVE-2026-107928 - gnutls: validate gnutls_record_send() return value
 Check the result code of gnutls_record_send() for sanity also in
 production builds. Previously the only check that the returned byte count
 does not exceed the requested length was a DEBUGASSERT(), which is compiled
 out in release builds; an oversized return value would underflow the
 remaining length and advance the buffer pointer out of bounds. Fail with
 CURLE_SEND_ERROR instead.
 .
 Backported to curl 8.14.1: gtls_send() here uses the older
 ssize_t/CURLcode *curlcode convention, so the error path sets *curlcode
 and returns -1 rather than returning CURLE_SEND_ERROR directly.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/64fb3e7a7b116f690966054f281624152d4a7651
Author: Stefan Eissing <stefan@eissing.org>
Last-Update: 2026-11-01
---
--- a/lib/vtls/gtls.c
+++ b/lib/vtls/gtls.c
@@ -1981,8 +1981,14 @@
       goto out;
     }
     nwritten = (size_t)rc;
+    if(nwritten > blen) {
+      DEBUGASSERT(0);
+      failf(data, "gnutls_record_send(len=%zu) returned %zd", blen, rc);
+      *curlcode = CURLE_SEND_ERROR;
+      rc = -1;
+      goto out;
+    }
     total_written += nwritten;
-    DEBUGASSERT(nwritten <= blen);
     buf = (char *)CURL_UNCONST(buf) + nwritten;
     blen -= nwritten;
   }
Description: CVE-2026-87862 - hsts: on load, only remove exact duplicates
 When loading an HSTS cache file, hsts_add() checked for an existing entry
 using Curl_hsts() with subdomain matching enabled for ".host" lines. A
 parent domain entry with includeSubDomains could therefore match a child
 entry, causing the child entry (possibly with a later expiry) to be treated
 as a duplicate and silently dropped, and the longer-lived entry to be lost.
 The fix looks up existing entries with subdomain matching disabled so only
 exact duplicates are merged.
 .
 Backport of the upstream change to hsts_add() in curl 8.14.1 (the upstream
 function hsts_add_host_expire() does not exist in this version). Includes
 the upstream regression test test3109.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/a1614c3bcf1593eb524b37792124357d97a5429c
Author: Daniel Stenberg <daniel@haxx.se>
Last-Update: 2026-11-01
---
--- a/lib/hsts.c
+++ b/lib/hsts.c
@@ -443,7 +443,7 @@ static CURLcode hsts_add(struct hsts *h, const char *line)
       subdomain = TRUE;
     }
     /* only add it if not already present */
-    e = Curl_hsts(h, curlx_str(&host), curlx_strlen(&host), subdomain);
+    e = Curl_hsts(h, curlx_str(&host), curlx_strlen(&host), FALSE);
     if(!e)
       result = hsts_create(h, curlx_str(&host), curlx_strlen(&host),
                            subdomain, expires);
