Description: CVE-2026-92386 - accept slightly longer lines in cookie jars
 When reading a cookie jar file, the per-line buffer was limited to
 MAX_COOKIE_LINE bytes, which is smaller than the longest cookie that
 Curl_cookie_add() accepts (name + value up to MAX_NAME plus attributes).
 A valid full-size cookie saved in a jar therefore exceeded the line
 buffer and aborted the file read. Allow the line buffer to be 48 bytes
 larger so that a full cookie fits.
 .
 Backported from upstream commit 445aa87e13f91c94bc742f54343a2eac924e1765 to
 curl 8.14.1, where the jar loading code lives in Curl_cookie_init() rather
 than cookie_load(). No upstream test accompanies the change.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/445aa87e13f91c94bc742f54343a2eac924e1765
Bug: https://github.com/curl/curl/pull/22964
Author: Daniel Stenberg <daniel@haxx.se>
Last-Update: 2026-10-31
---
