Description: CVE-2026-82209 - cookies set for an exact PSL domain are host-only
 A cookie set by a server for a domain that is itself an exact entry in the
 Public Suffix List (e.g. "github.io") was stored as a tailmatching cookie.
 This allowed such a cookie to be sent to arbitrary subdomains
 (e.g. "attacker.github.io"), leaking a cookie set for a public suffix to
 unrelated hosts. This backport marks a cookie that is set for an exact PSL
 domain as host-only (clears co->tailmatch) and moves the public-suffix check
 earlier in Curl_cookie_add() so the corrected tailmatch flag is applied
 before the __Host- prefix validation. Added test 2318 to verify; test1136
 expected output updated accordingly.
 .
 Backported from upstream commit 95c1e8915dce64606bd753fd47fc0bd236e31cd6 to
 curl 8.14.1; the is_public_suffix() helper in this version returns an int
 (CERR_*) and takes a non-const Cookie, so the tailmatch clearing hunk was
 adapted to the local shape. The upstream test798 change is omitted because
 test798 does not exist in this target tree.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/95c1e8915dce64606bd753fd47fc0bd236e31cd6
Bug: https://github.com/curl/curl/issues/22730
Author: Daniel Stenberg <daniel@haxx.se>
Last-Update: 2026-09-09
---
--- a/lib/cookie.c
+++ b/lib/cookie.c
@@ -914,6 +914,13 @@ is_public_suffix(struct Curl_easy *data,
         Curl_strntolower(lcase, domain, dlen + 1);
         Curl_strntolower(lcookie, co->domain, clen + 1);
         acceptable = psl_is_cookie_domain_acceptable(psl, lcase, lcookie);
+
+        /* if the cookie is acceptable, but is set for a PSL domain, then it
+           cannot be tailmatching */
+        if(acceptable && co->tailmatch &&
+           curl_strequal(co->domain, domain) &&
+           psl_is_public_suffix(psl, lcookie))
+          co->tailmatch = FALSE;
         Curl_psl_release(data);
       }
       else
@@ -1089,6 +1096,9 @@ Curl_cookie_add(struct Curl_easy *data,
     /* The __Secure- prefix only requires that the cookie be set secure */
     goto fail;

+  if(is_public_suffix(data, co, domain))
+    goto fail;
+
   if(co->prefix_host) {
     /*
      * The __Host- prefix requires the cookie to be secure, have a "/" path
@@ -1118,9 +1128,6 @@ Curl_cookie_add(struct Curl_easy *data,
   if(!noexpire)
     remove_expired(ci);

-  if(is_public_suffix(data, co, domain))
-    goto fail;
-
   if(replace_existing(data, co, ci, secure, &replaces))
     goto fail;

