Description: CVE-2026-92390 - tool: buffer headers before remote filename selection
 With --remote-header-name (-J) and --show-headers (-i), curl opened the
 output file as soon as a header that bypassed the Content-Disposition
 handling arrived (informational 1xx responses such as 103 Early Hints, or an
 ETag header consumed by --etag-save). The output file was thus created or
 truncated under the URL-derived name before the Content-Disposition filename
 was known, which could clobber an unrelated file. Buffer such headers until
 the filename decision is complete, via a shared buffer_header() helper and
 a cd_checked flag in tool_header_cb(). Includes tests 3037 and 3038.
 .
 Backported to curl 8.14.1: uses the local aprintf()/free() idiom instead of
 curlx_memdup0()/curlx_free(), and sets cd_checked at the end of the existing
 honor_cd_filename branch.
