Description: CVE-2026-19931 - do not reuse Negotiate/NTLM connections authenticated with ambient (empty) credentials
 libcurl improperly reused an HTTP connection that had been authenticated via
 Negotiate (GSSAPI on Unix, SSPI on Windows) or NTLM using a blank/ambient
 username. Because the ambient identity can be switched outside libcurl's
 knowledge between requests, a later request issued by a different local user
 could be sent over a previous user's already-authenticated connection,
 leaking one user's authenticated session to another (CWE-488, TOCTOU).
 .
 This backports the root-cause guard from the upstream fix to curl 8.14.1,
 which predates the connection-pool "admin handle" / Curl_creds refactor that
 the full upstream commit is built on. A connection whose Negotiate or NTLM
 handshake was performed with an empty username is now refused for reuse in
 the connection-matching path (url_match_conn) unless it is the exact
 connection this transfer used before (data->state.lastconnect_id ==
 conn->connection_id), mirroring upstream's url_allow_sspi_empty_creds logic
 (which commit 7103a93b switched to key on the last-used connection id).
 .
 The upstream in-patch test1554 change only adjusts SHARE/CONNECT mutex trace
 output produced by the larger share-locking refactor and does not exercise
 the credential-reuse guard, so it is intentionally not carried over.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/7103a93b05bc69ea98ed9d05d02fa9eeba533f2f
Bug: https://curl.se/docs/CVE-2026-19931.html
Author: Stefan Eissing <stefan@eissing.org>
Last-Update: 2026-09-09
---
--- a/lib/url.c
+++ b/lib/url.c
@@ -1239,6 +1239,53 @@ static bool url_match_auth_ntlm(struct connectdata *conn,
