Description: CVE-2026-87864 - imap: APPEND CRLF fix
 Deny an IMAP APPEND operation with CRLF conversion requested, as the final
 upload size cannot be predicted and APPEND requires announcing it before
 the upload starts. The unknown-size check existed, but the CRLF conversion
 that turns a known size into an unknown one was not accounted for. Compute
 the size from all client readers via Curl_creader_total_length().
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/3b547de301342b347fb3c6ea6ae7979070793a66
Author: Stefan Eissing <stefan@eissing.org>
Last-Update: 2026-11-01
---
--- a/lib/imap.c
+++ b/lib/imap.c
@@ -887,7 +887,6 @@ static CURLcode imap_perform_append(stru
       result = Curl_creader_set_mime(data, &data->set.mimepost);
     if(result)
       return result;
-    data->state.infilesize = Curl_creader_client_length(data);
   }
   else
 #endif
@@ -897,9 +896,15 @@ static CURLcode imap_perform_append(stru
       return result;
   }
 
-  /* Check we know the size of the upload */
+  /* Check we know the size of the upload. This takes all readers
+   * into account. Especially crlf conversions which make the size
+   * unpredictable, e.g. -1. */
+  data->state.infilesize = Curl_creader_total_length(data);
   if(data->state.infilesize < 0) {
-    failf(data, "Cannot APPEND with unknown input file size");
+    if(data->set.crlf)
+      failf(data, "Cannot APPEND with CRLF conversion making size unknown");
+    else
+      failf(data, "Cannot APPEND with unknown input file size");
     return CURLE_UPLOAD_FAILED;
   }
 
Description: CVE-2026-11856 - digest: flush state on origin or credential change
 Backport of upstream commit 5c6b4880357ab3e72967c1c45cae0f96ffabc535
 ("digest: flush state on origin or credential change").
 .
 Re-engineered for curl 8.14.1 which predates the PEERS abstraction
 (Curl_peer_*/Curl_creds_* helpers, struct Curl_peer/Curl_creds, and
 data->conn->origin / data->state.creds did not yet exist). The 8.14.1
 backport caches the origin as "scheme://host:port" plus the active
 credentials (state.aptr.user / state.aptr.passwd) on struct digestdata,
 taken from data->conn (the live connection), and calls
 Curl_auth_digest_cleanup() when either tuple changes between transfers
 on the same handle. This prevents the captured Authorization: header
 (computed for hostA + userA) from being re-used against hostB or with
 different credentials -- the cross-origin Digest auth state leak
 described in CVE-2026-11856.
 .
 NOTE: An earlier draft of this backport incorrectly snapshotted
 data->state.first_host / first_remote_port / first_remote_protocol.
 Those fields are only allocated for Location-follow auth scoping and are
 never populated for ordinary handle reuse in 8.14.1, so origin changes
 would not have been detected. This revision matches the bookworm
 backport semantics and uses data->conn->handler/host/remote_port.
 .
 Validated by paired test 1686 ported to the curl 8.14.1 libtest
 framework (test.h / CURLcode test(char *URL) signature, lib1686_SOURCES
 wired up in tests/libtest/Makefile.inc).
Origin: backport, https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/5c6b4880357ab3e72967c1c45cae0f96ffabc535
Bug: https://curl.se/docs/CVE-2026-11856.html
Author: Daniel Stenberg <daniel@haxx.se>
Last-Update: 2026-07-27
