Description: CVE-2026-80229 - openssl: avoid conn reuse if provider is used
 When an OpenSSL provider or engine is in use (indicated by a non-NULL
 per-transfer OpenSSL library context, data->state.libctx), the resulting
 SSL context carries provider/engine state that must not be shared across
 unrelated transfers via connection reuse. Reusing such a connection can
 lead to using the wrong cryptographic material. Forbid connection reuse
 in that case by marking the connection for closure.
 .
 This backports upstream commit 7ea37abc6ac0120ba5f6d94be8d196f7cf1506bb,
 adapting the connclose() call to the two-argument (reason-string) form
 used by this curl version.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/7ea37abc6ac0120ba5f6d94be8d196f7cf1506bb
