Description: CVE-2026-13608 - openldap: handle Curl_sasl_continue() returns better
 When performing SASL authentication over LDAP, oldap_state_sasl_resp()
 only stopped the state machine when the SASL exchange was no longer in
 progress. It did not account for the SASL_IDLE result, which indicates
 that no authentication mechanism remained after a cancellation. This
 could leave the connection in an inconsistent authentication state.
 .
 This patch handles the Curl_sasl_continue() progress return codes
 explicitly: SASL_DONE stops the state machine (authenticated), while
 SASL_IDLE reports the authentication as cancelled and denies the login
 with CURLE_LOGIN_DENIED.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/ea71c3b6b60e563651ea8596a975aef0c8199519
Author: Daniel Stenberg <daniel@haxx.se>
Last-Update: 2026-09-09
